From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 01:07:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: allow selecting the self-update repository

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: let fork builds check and install updates from a selected GitHub repository
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none

Patch intent:
Add a validated JCODE_UPDATE_REPO override for GitHub release, main-channel,
source-bootstrap, and development-build self-update operations.

Why it exists:
Fork maintainers need release binaries and source bootstrap updates to follow
their published releases without redirecting unrelated runtime network traffic
or checked-out Git remotes.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-app-core/src/update.rs owns release lookup, main checks, source
bootstrap, and prepared update installation. update_dev_guard.rs owns the
GitHub ancestry comparison. jcode-update-core::PreparedUpdate carries the
selected source repository across background installation.

Update guidance:
Keep repository input GitHub-slug-only and validated before URL or clone
construction. Preserve configured checkout upstreams and retain the selected
repository throughout a prepared source update. Fork releases must keep the
expected platform assets and optional SHA256SUMS asset.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-app-core update_repository --lib
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-app-core github_comparison_uses_selected_update_repository --lib
scripts/cargo_exec.sh check -p jcode-app-core
